# SwiftPM does not check a package out from its origin. It first creates a local mirror under
# SourcePackages/repositories and then clones the working copy from that directory, so the
# checkout's remote is a path on disk and git-lfs derives no LFS endpoint from it: every object
# fails to smudge with "remote missing object". That is invisible on a machine whose mirror has
# accumulated the objects and fatal on a clean one, which is what CI runs on.
#
# Naming the server here overrides the derivation, so LFS keeps working for anything consuming
# this package through SwiftPM. Update it if the repository ever moves.
[lfs]
	url = https://github.com/tr1ckyf0x-studio/FoxDebug.git/info/lfs
